# QM5_11558 Carter-T M5 — PSAR + MACD(64,128,9) + EMA(100) (M5)

## Source
- Source: Thomas Carter, "20 Forex Trading Strategies (5 Minute Time Frame)", System #19, self-published 2014. URL/local PDF: `C:\Users\Administrator\Dropbox\Finanzen\Forex\###  Forex to read\367145560-20-forex-trading-strategies-5-minute-time-frame-pdf.pdf`

## Mechanics

**Concept**: EMA(100) defines trend bias. PSAR confirms directional momentum. MACD(64,128,9) uses doubled periods from standard (64=2×32, 128=2×64) for a slower, smoother signal on M5. All three must align. TP: 7–12 pips; SL: 3 pips beyond first PSAR dot (tight stop).

**PSAR parameter note**: Source lists "(0.01-0.01)" which appears to mean step=0.01, max=0.01 — physically unlikely (PSAR wouldn't accelerate). P2 assumes (0.01, 0.1): slow PSAR (slow to accelerate). P3 sweeps include (0.02, 0.2).

### Entry
**LONG**: `iClose[1] > iMA(100)[1]` AND `iSAR(0.01,0.1,1) < iLow[1]` AND `iMACD(64,128,9,MAIN,1) > 0`
**SHORT**: `iClose[1] < iMA(100)[1]` AND `iSAR > iHigh[1]` AND `iMACD(...,MAIN,1) < 0`

### Exit
- **SL**: 3 pips below/above the first PSAR dot after entry
- **TP**: 9 pips (midpoint of 7-12 range)

### Stop Loss
- `SL = 3*pip + MathAbs(iClose[entry] - iSAR[entry])`; P2 cap: 15 pips

### Position Sizing
- `RISK_FIXED = $1000` for P2. `RISK_PERCENT = 0.5%` for live.

### Additional filters
- Timeframe: M5; Instruments: EURUSD.DWX, GBPUSD.DWX, AUDUSD.DWX; Spread cap: 5p; No Friday entry

